  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.65,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.8,
    "rationale": "At 18 h the undiluted reading was 1.553. The diluted aliquots, scaled back by their dilution factor, read higher: 3x gave 1.615, 10x gave 1.654 (two replicates, 0.168 and 0.163), and 30x gave 1.656 (two noisy replicates, 0.050 and 0.060). Scaled readings rise with dilution and then level off at about 1.65, which is the pattern of a reader losing linearity at high density. The undiluted reading is therefore about 6% below the proportional value. The 12 h aliquot at 10x gave 1.681 scaled, against 1.604 undiluted, which agrees with this. The undiluted plateau at about 1.6 from 7 h onward is flattened by this compression. The offset is modest, and the 30x replicates are noisy, so confidence is not very high."
  },
